Chapter: PropArith

 Arithmetic inside a proposition. A proposition is parsed by
 parse-type, and until this shipped the type grammar had no infix
 operators, so `1 + 1 === 2` stopped at the operator: the grammar
 returned the bare `1`, the claim parser read the `+` as the proof
 name, and the failure surfaced as CDX1000 on the token after it.

 The operator is an ordinary application spine now, which is the shape
 the proof normalizer already reduces, so each claim below is folded to
 a literal and checked by Refl rather than admitted on faith. The
 negative guard is codex/test/errors/prop-arith-false.

 The precedence claim is the one that can fail. A single
 left-associative loop reads `1 + 2 * 3` as `(1 + 2) * 3`, which is 9,
 so admitting 7 is what says the multiplicative level binds first.

Section: Claims

  claim lit-control : 2 === 2
  proof lit-control = Refl
  qed

  claim add : 1 + 1 === 2
  proof add = Refl
  qed

  claim sub : 5 - 3 === 2
  proof sub = Refl
  qed

  claim mul : 2 * 3 === 6
  proof mul = Refl
  qed

  claim divide : 8 / 4 === 2
  proof divide = Refl
  qed

  claim nested : 1 + 2 + 3 === 6
  proof nested = Refl
  qed

  claim precedence : 1 + 2 * 3 === 7
  proof precedence = Refl
  qed

Section: Signed Literals

 A negative literal is one atom, not a minus applied to something.
 Before that shipped, `parse-type-atom`'s catch-all took the bare `-`
 and left the digits behind, so `-2` could not sit on either side of a
 `===` and the normalizer had to refuse to fold any negative result --
 folding one would have named a literal the grammar could not write.

 `sub-neg` is the claim that needs both halves at once: the left side
 folds to a negative and the right side has to parse as one.

  claim bare-neg : -2 === -2
  proof bare-neg = Refl
  qed

  claim sub-neg : 1 - 3 === -2
  proof sub-neg = Refl
  qed

  claim zero-sub : 0 - 5 === -5
  proof zero-sub = Refl
  qed

  claim neg-operand : -2 + 5 === 3
  proof neg-operand = Refl
  qed

  claim neg-mul : -2 * 3 === -6
  proof neg-mul = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "prop-arith ok"
  end
